export default [{"id":"k1","title":"About Visionbotix","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Visionbotix is an AI-first product engineering studio. We build AI agents that do real work, plus the web, mobile and SaaS software they run in, with security built in."},{"id":"k2","title":"Visionbotix: Facts","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Facts: founded 2020; team of 30; 50+ projects delivered by our team for clients in 20 countries, including the USA, the UK, Germany, Switzerland, Austria, Australia, New Zealand, the UAE. Office: 2nd Floor, Meridian Software Technology Park, Satellite Town, Murree Road, Rawalpindi, Pakistan. Legal name: Visionbotix SMC-Private Limited. Founder: Sikandar Farooq."},{"id":"k3","title":"Visionbotix: Contact","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Contact: info@visionbotix.com · +92 51 8896050 · https://visionbotix.com/contact/ (fixed quote within 24 hours of a call)."},{"id":"k4","title":"Visionbotix: Pricing","url":"https://visionbotix.com/pricing/","text":"Pricing (USD, \"from\"): packaged AI agents from $750 setup + $199/month; AI Opportunity Audit $490; dedicated engineers from $2,200/month, hourly from $25. Details: https://visionbotix.com/pricing/"},{"id":"k5","title":"Visionbotix: Typical project costs","url":"https://visionbotix.com/estimate/","text":"Typical project costs (indicative ranges from our price list; a fixed quote follows a call): business website or simple web app $4,500–$7,000 (4–6 weeks); web app with accounts, payments and an admin $12,000–$18,000 (6–10 weeks); mobile app for ios and android $17,900–$27,000 (7–12 weeks); saas mvp with subscriptions $24,100–$36,000 (8–13 weeks); ai chatbot over your documents $7,500–$11,500 (5–8 weeks); custom ai agent that uses your systems $14,500–$22,000 (7–11 weeks); computer vision or iot prototype $10,000–$15,000 (5–8 weeks); clinic front desk (3 ai agents) $3,000–$4,000 setup + $699/mo (live in 2–5 weeks). Estimator: https://visionbotix.com/estimate/"},{"id":"k6","title":"Visionbotix: Promises","url":"https://visionbotix.com/about/","text":"Promises: NDA from the first call; the client owns 100% of the code and IP; fixed price or monthly, paid by milestone; overlap hours with the US, UK, Europe, the Gulf and Australia; weekly demos; 30 days of post-launch support."},{"id":"k7","title":"Packaged AI agents: Receptionist Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $349/mo. Our Receptionist Agent is an AI voice receptionist that answers your phone line 24/7 in your business's voice. It answers questions, books, moves and cancels appointments in your calendar or practice system, takes messages and puts urgent calls through to a person. Clinics, dental practices, salons and home-service firms go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k8","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: How is an AI receptionist different from an answering service or a phone menu? A: An answering service takes a message and a phone menu makes callers press buttons. An AI receptionist holds a real conversation, answers questions from your own information and books the appointment during the call, at any hour and on several calls at once. Q: Will callers know they are speaking to an AI? A: Yes. We configure a clear, friendly disclosure in the greeting, and callers can ask for a person at any time. Being upfront builds trust and keeps you on the right side of disclosure rules."},{"id":"k9","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: What happens with urgent or complicated calls? A: You decide the rules. Calls that match them, such as urgent symptoms, complaints or a request for a named person, are transferred live or flagged to your on-call team by text with a short summary, so a human takes over. Q: Can it use my existing phone number? A: Yes. You keep your number and forward calls to the agent, either all calls, only after hours or only when your lines are busy. We can also set up a new local number in most countries."},{"id":"k10","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Which calendars and practice systems does it work with? A: Google Calendar, Outlook, Calendly and Cal.com out of the box, plus practice and CRM systems such as Open Dental, Cliniko, HubSpot and Salesforce. If your system has an API, we can connect it. Q: Which languages does it speak? A: English by default, with natural accents. Arabic, Urdu, Spanish, German, French and other major languages are available, and the agent can switch language when the caller does."},{"id":"k11","title":"Receptionist Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-receptionist/","text":"Q: Is it suitable for healthcare data under HIPAA or UK GDPR? A: Yes, with the right setup. We keep data in your chosen region, encrypt it, apply your retention rules and, for US healthcare, use providers that sign a BAA. We document the data flow so your compliance lead can sign it off."},{"id":"k12","title":"Packaged AI agents: Support Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Price: From $2,500 + $449/mo. Our Support Agent is an AI customer support agent that resolves tier-1 tickets on website chat, email and WhatsApp, 24/7. It answers from your help center, policies and order data, handles actions like order lookups and returns, and hands anything sensitive to your team with full context. Online stores, SaaS and service businesses go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k13","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: How is an AI customer support agent different from a chatbot? A: A classic chatbot follows a decision tree and breaks as soon as a question doesn't fit it. An AI support agent understands free-text questions, answers from your own docs and can take actions in your systems, such as looking up an order or starting a return, then hands off when it should. Q: What stops it from making things up? A: It answers only from the sources you approve, such as your help center, policies and order data, and attaches the source to each answer. If the answer isn't in those sources, it says so and passes the ticket to your team. We test it on your real past tickets before launch."},{"id":"k14","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: What happens when it can't solve the problem? A: It hands the conversation to the right queue in your help desk with a short summary, the customer details and what it already tried, so your agent doesn't start from zero. Customers can also ask for a person at any time. Q: Does it work with our help desk? A: Yes. We connect Zendesk, Freshdesk, Intercom, HubSpot, Gorgias, Help Scout and Salesforce Service Cloud, and the agent works inside your existing queues and tags. If your system has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k15","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: Which languages does it support? A: English by default, plus Arabic, Urdu, Spanish, French, German and other major languages. It replies in the language the customer writes in, and answers still come from your approved docs. Q: Will it replace my support team? A: No. It takes the repetitive tier-1 tickets so your team can spend its time on complex cases, upset customers and the conversations that keep accounts. Refunds and other sensitive actions still need a person to approve them."},{"id":"k16","title":"Support Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-customer-support-agent/","text":"Q: How much work is setup for my team? A: Expect a kickoff call, access to your help desk and docs, and a few short review sessions while we test it on real tickets. We do the configuration, connections and testing."},{"id":"k17","title":"Packaged AI agents: WhatsApp Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $299/mo. Our WhatsApp Agent is an AI agent for the WhatsApp Business Platform and Instagram DMs. It replies in seconds in English, Arabic, Urdu and more, answers product questions from your catalog, shares live order status, follows up abandoned carts with approved templates and passes complex chats to your team. Online stores, clinics and service brands go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k18","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Is this allowed by WhatsApp, and could my number get banned? A: We build on the official WhatsApp Business Platform, not unofficial automation tools, which is what puts numbers at risk. We follow Meta's rules on opt-in, the 24-hour reply window and approved templates, and we watch your quality rating so marketing messages stay welcome. Q: Can it reply in Arabic and Urdu? A: Yes. It replies in the language the customer writes in, including Arabic, Urdu and Roman Urdu, as well as English and other major languages. Answers still come from your approved catalog and policies, and we review the tone in each language with you."},{"id":"k19","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Can I keep my existing WhatsApp number? A: In most cases, yes. We connect your number to the WhatsApp Business Platform, and depending on your setup you can keep using the WhatsApp Business app on the same number alongside the agent. If that doesn't suit, we set up a new number for you. Q: What happens when a customer wants a real person? A: They can ask at any time. The chat moves to your team's shared inbox with the full history and order details, and the agent stays quiet until your team hands it back."},{"id":"k20","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: Does it also work on Instagram? A: Yes. The same agent answers Instagram direct messages with the same catalog, rules and handoff, so customers get the same answer wherever they ask. Q: Which stores and couriers does it connect to? A: Shopify, WooCommerce, Magento, Salla and Zid out of the box, plus couriers such as Aramex and DHL Express. If your store or courier has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k21","title":"WhatsApp Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/whatsapp-ai-agent/","text":"Q: What if it gives a customer a wrong answer? A: It only answers from your store data and approved knowledge base, and every chat is logged so you can see exactly what it said and why. When you correct a fact, the fix applies to every future conversation, and we review chats with you weekly."},{"id":"k22","title":"Packaged AI agents: Booking Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $299/mo. Our Booking Agent is an AI appointment setter that contacts every new lead from your forms, ads and portals within 60 seconds, by text, WhatsApp or call. It asks your qualifying questions, books qualified leads into the right calendar, sends reminders to cut no-shows and logs everything in your CRM. Real estate, clinic and home-service teams go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k23","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: How is the Booking Agent different from the AI Receptionist? A: The Receptionist answers calls that come in to you. The Booking Agent reaches out to new leads from your forms, ads and portals within 60 seconds, qualifies them and books the appointment. Many businesses use both, one for inbound calls and one for speed-to-lead. Q: Is it legal to text and call leads automatically? A: It can be, when the lead has given the right consent. We set the agent up to contact only leads with consent on record, to name your business, respect quiet hours and honor opt-outs immediately, following TCPA in the US and GDPR and PECR in the UK and EU. Your legal advisor should confirm the consent wording on your forms."},{"id":"k24","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: Will leads know they are talking to an AI? A: Yes, if they ask, and you can add a short disclosure to the first message. The agent never claims to be a person, and anyone can ask to speak to your team at any time. Q: Which lead sources and CRMs does it work with? A: Meta, Google and TikTok lead forms, your website forms, and CRMs such as HubSpot, Salesforce, GoHighLevel, Follow Up Boss, Zoho and Pipedrive. Portals that send leads by email or webhook can be connected too. If your system has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k25","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: What happens if a lead asks something the agent can't answer? A: It tells the lead a team member will follow up, logs the question in your CRM and alerts the right person. It does not guess prices, availability or terms that are not in your approved information. Q: Can it call leads as well as text them? A: Yes. You choose the channel per source, for example a text first and a call if there is no reply, or a call straight away for high-value leads. Calls use a natural voice and can be transferred live to your team."},{"id":"k26","title":"Booking Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-booking-agent/","text":"Q: Which languages does it work in? A: English by default, plus Arabic, Urdu, Spanish, French and other major languages. It can follow the language the lead uses on the form or in their reply."},{"id":"k27","title":"Packaged AI agents: SDR Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Price: From $2,500 + $499/mo. Our SDR Agent is an AI sales development rep for B2B teams. It researches each target account, finds the right contacts, writes personalized emails and LinkedIn drafts, handles replies and books meetings into your reps' calendars, with everything logged in your CRM. Your team approves every sequence before it sends. SaaS companies and agencies go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k28","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: Will prospects know the emails were written with AI? A: Every email is reviewed and approved by your rep and sent from their inbox, so it is your team's message. When the agent handles replies, it never claims to be a person if asked, and you can add a short disclosure if you prefer. Q: Will it hurt our email deliverability? A: It's designed to protect it. We set daily sending limits, warm up inboxes, use suppression lists and keep volumes steady, and because each email is specific to the account, it reads like a real message, not a blast. We can also set up separate sending domains so your main domain stays clean."},{"id":"k29","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: How personalized is the outreach really? A: Each first email is built on research about that account, such as a new location, an open role or a recent announcement, and connects it to a problem you solve. Your rep sees the research behind every draft and can edit anything before approving. Q: Does it automate LinkedIn? A: No. Automating LinkedIn accounts breaks LinkedIn's terms and puts your reps' profiles at risk. The agent drafts LinkedIn messages and connection notes for your reps to send themselves."},{"id":"k30","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: Which CRMs and data providers does it work with? A: HubSpot, Salesforce, Pipedrive and Close for CRM, Apollo.io and Hunter for contact data, and Outreach or Salesloft if you already use them for sequencing. If your tool has an API, we can connect it. Q: Is cold B2B outreach allowed under GDPR? A: In many cases, yes, when it is relevant to the person's role, identifies your company, offers an easy opt-out and rests on a documented legitimate interest. We build those safeguards in, and your legal advisor should confirm the approach for your markets."},{"id":"k31","title":"SDR Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-sdr-agent/","text":"Q: What if it writes something wrong or off-brand? A: Nothing goes out without your rep's approval, and the agent only uses the claims and proof points you've signed off. When you edit a draft, we feed that back into the style guide so the next batch is closer to your voice."},{"id":"k32","title":"Packaged AI agents: Social Media Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,000 + $399/mo. Our Social Media Agent is an AI social media manager for businesses that need to post often but lack time. It plans a content calendar, writes captions, prepares on-brand graphics, schedules posts across your accounts and replies to comments and DMs in your voice. You approve the calendar, and sensitive replies go to your staff. Live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k33","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: How is an AI social media manager different from a scheduling tool like Buffer? A: A scheduler publishes what you give it. The agent also plans the calendar, writes the captions, prepares the graphics and answers comments and DMs. If you already use a scheduler, it can publish through it. Q: Will the posts sound like AI wrote them? A: We build a written voice guide from your best past posts and your feedback, and the agent drafts against it. You approve the calendar, so anything that doesn't sound like you is changed before it goes out, and we fold your edits back into the guide during weekly tuning."},{"id":"k34","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: Does it replace my social media manager or agency? A: It replaces the repetitive part, which is drafting, resizing, scheduling and first replies. Many teams keep a person for strategy, shoots and community moments, and that person spends their time on ideas instead of admin. Q: What happens if it replies with something wrong? A: Replies only use facts from your approved knowledge base, and anything sensitive, such as complaints, refunds or health and legal questions, goes to staff instead of getting an answer. Every reply is logged, so you can edit or delete it, and we fix the rule behind it in weekly tuning."},{"id":"k35","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: Which platforms does it support? A: Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok, X, YouTube, Pinterest and Google Business Profile, through their official APIs. Some features, such as DM replies on certain platforms, depend on what each platform allows for business accounts. Q: Is this allowed under the platforms' rules? A: Yes. It posts and replies through official business APIs with your permission, and it never buys engagement, runs fake accounts or sends unsolicited mass DMs. It also labels AI-generated images where a platform asks for it."},{"id":"k36","title":"Social Media Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-social-media-agent/","text":"Q: Can it create images and video? A: It produces graphics, carousels and simple motion from your brand templates and photos. For product shots and video it works best with real footage you supply, which it trims, captions and resizes for each platform."},{"id":"k37","title":"Packaged AI agents: SEO & GEO Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $499/mo. Our SEO & GEO Agent is an AI SEO agent that covers classic search and generative engine optimization (GEO). It finds ranking and content gaps, drafts pages for your editor, flags technical fixes, and tracks how ChatGPT, Perplexity, Google AI Overviews and Copilot cite your brand. Built for B2B, SaaS, e-commerce and local businesses; live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k38","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: What is GEO, and how is it different from SEO? A: SEO helps your pages rank in classic search results. Generative engine optimization (GEO) helps AI assistants such as ChatGPT, Perplexity and Google AI Overviews understand, mention and cite your business when they answer a question. The foundations overlap, and GEO adds tracking of AI answers and pages written to be quoted. Q: Can you guarantee rankings or AI citations? A: No, and nobody honestly can, because search engines and AI assistants decide what to show. What we commit to is the process, which is regular tracking, a prioritized task list, reviewed drafts and technical fixes, with a weekly report that shows what changed."},{"id":"k39","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: Will AI-written content hurt my site? A: Thin, mass-produced content can. The agent drafts pages around your real expertise, facts and examples, and an editor reviews every page before it is published. It never publishes in bulk on its own. Q: How do you track mentions in ChatGPT and Perplexity? A: We run a fixed set of buyer questions on a schedule across the major assistants and record whether you are mentioned, how you are described and which URLs are cited. AI answers vary from run to run, so we report trends over several weeks rather than a single result."},{"id":"k40","title":"SEO & GEO Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-seo-agent/","text":"Q: Does it replace my SEO agency or in-house marketer? A: It replaces the repetitive work of crawling, monitoring, research and first drafts. Strategy, subject expertise and final editing stay with your team or agency, who get more done because the groundwork is ready. Q: Which tools and CMS does it work with? A: Google Search Console, Analytics 4 and Business Profile, Bing Webmaster Tools, Ahrefs or Semrush if you use them, and WordPress, Webflow, Shopify or a Git-based site for drafts and fixes. If your CMS has an API, we can connect it."},{"id":"k41","title":"Packaged AI agents: Ads Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Price: From $1,500 + $449/mo. Our Ads Agent is an AI ads agent that reviews your Meta and Google Ads accounts every morning. It spots wasted spend, pauses ads that break your rules, catches tracking problems and proposes budget moves. Anything above the thresholds you set waits for your approval. Built for e-commerce brands, lead-gen businesses and marketing teams; live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k42","title":"Ads Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Q: Will it improve my ROAS? A: We don't promise ad results, because they depend on your offer, creative, market and budget. What the agent does is make sure no account goes a day without a check, losing ads are caught early and every budget move is backed by data you can see. Q: Can it spend my money without asking? A: Only within the limits you set. You decide what it may pause or shift on its own, per account and per day, and everything above that waits for your approval. It can never raise your total budget or touch billing."},{"id":"k43","title":"Ads Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Q: How is this different from Google's and Meta's own automation? A: Platform automation optimizes inside one platform toward the goal you give it. The agent sits above both platforms, checks results against your business targets and real sales data, explains every proposal in plain language and asks before big changes. It works alongside Smart Bidding and Advantage+, not against them. Q: Does it replace my agency or media buyer? A: No. It takes over the daily watching and the paperwork, so your media buyer or agency spends time on strategy, creative and testing. Agencies also use it to check every client account each morning."},{"id":"k44","title":"Ads Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-ads-agent/","text":"Q: Which ad platforms does it support? A: Meta (Facebook and Instagram) and Google Ads out of the box, with Microsoft Advertising, LinkedIn Ads and TikTok Ads on request. It can also read GA4, Shopify or your CRM so it judges results by real sales or leads. Q: What if it makes a wrong call? A: Every action is logged with the before and after values, so any change can be reviewed and reversed quickly. You can also keep it in shadow mode, where it only proposes, until you trust its judgment."},{"id":"k45","title":"Packaged AI agents: Reputation Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Price: From $750 + $199/mo. Our Reputation Agent is an AI reputation management agent that watches your Google, Trustpilot and app-store reviews around the clock. It drafts specific, on-brand replies, holds negative reviews for your approval, alerts you to urgent issues and asks every recent customer for a review, within platform rules. Clinics, restaurants, hotels, online stores and apps go live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k46","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: Is it allowed to use AI to reply to reviews? A: Yes. Google, Trustpilot and the app stores let businesses reply to reviews, and what matters is that replies are honest, relevant and respectful. We keep a person in the loop for every negative or sensitive reply, and you can require approval for all of them. Q: Can it remove or hide bad reviews? A: No, and nothing should. Genuine reviews stay up. The agent can flag reviews that appear to break platform policy, such as spam or reviews of the wrong business, so you can report them through the platform's own process."},{"id":"k47","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: Can it ask only happy customers for reviews? A: No. Asking only satisfied customers, known as review gating, is against Google's policies and FTC guidance in the US, and so are incentives for reviews. The agent asks every eligible customer in the same way, which keeps your profile trustworthy and your listing safe. Q: Which review platforms does it cover? A: Google Business Profile, Trustpilot, the App Store, Google Play and Facebook out of the box. Other platforms can be added where they offer an official API or review notifications, and where a platform doesn't allow replies through its API, the agent drafts the reply and your team posts it."},{"id":"k48","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: Will the replies sound robotic or repetitive? A: No. Each reply responds to what the reviewer actually wrote, follows your style guide and varies its wording. You can edit any draft, and your edits shape future replies. Q: How does it handle healthcare privacy? A: For clinics and practices, replies never confirm that the reviewer is a patient, mention treatment or share any details, even if the reviewer did. Negative reviews are always held for approval, and data stays in your chosen region."},{"id":"k49","title":"Reputation Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-reputation-agent/","text":"Q: What if it drafts something wrong? A: Sensitive replies don't post without a person approving them, and every draft, edit and approval is logged. If you correct a fact or a phrase, we add it to the style guide so it doesn't happen again."},{"id":"k50","title":"Packaged AI agents: Knowledge Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Price: From $3,500 + $399/mo. Our Knowledge Agent is a private AI knowledge assistant that answers your team's questions from your own documents, wiki, shared drives and tickets. Every answer cites its sources, and people only see what their existing permissions allow. It runs in your private cloud or on-premise for sensitive data. Built for operations, support, legal and engineering teams; live in 2–4 weeks."},{"id":"k51","title":"Knowledge Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Q: How does it avoid making things up? A: It uses retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), so it first finds the relevant passages in your documents and then answers only from them, citing each source. If the sources don't cover the question, it says it doesn't know. No AI is perfect, which is why every answer carries citations people can check in one click. Q: How is this different from ChatGPT Enterprise or Microsoft Copilot? A: Those are strong general assistants. The Knowledge Agent is built around your sources, with retrieval tuned to your documents, permissions mirrored across tools from different vendors, gap reports for document owners and the option to run fully on-premise. It can also run alongside Copilot."},{"id":"k52","title":"Knowledge Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Q: Can it run fully on-premise or air-gapped? A: Yes. We can deploy on your own servers with an open-weight model, so no document, question or answer leaves your network. Hosted models are stronger on some tasks, so we help you choose per use case. Q: Will people see documents they shouldn't? A: No. Permissions are checked at question time against your identity provider and each source's own access rules, so an answer can only draw on files that person can already open."},{"id":"k53","title":"Knowledge Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-knowledge-assistant/","text":"Q: Which sources can it connect to? A: SharePoint, OneDrive, Google Drive, Confluence, Notion, Jira, Zendesk, Box, Dropbox, GitHub and network file shares, plus databases and internal systems with an API. Scanned PDFs are read with OCR. Q: How much work is it for our team? A: A few hours in total, covering a kick-off call, access to the sources and a small group to test answers during setup. After launch, document owners spend a little time each month on the gap report."},{"id":"k54","title":"Packaged AI agents: Document Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Price: From $3,000 + $399/mo. Our Document Agent handles AI document processing for finance, operations and compliance teams. It reads invoices, receipts, contracts, claims and KYC documents from email, scans or uploads, extracts the fields you need, checks them against your rules and ERP data, and posts clean records. Anything uncertain goes to a human review queue. Live in 2–4 weeks."},{"id":"k55","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: How accurate is it? A: It depends on the document type and scan quality, so we measure it on a sample of your own past documents during setup and show you the results before go-live. Fields the agent is unsure about are never posted silently; they go to a person in the review queue. Q: How is this different from OCR software? A: OCR turns an image into text. The agent understands what the text means, so it finds the invoice number or renewal date in any layout, checks it against your rules and data, and posts the result. Template-based OCR needs a new template for each layout, and the agent does not."},{"id":"k56","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: What happens when it gets something wrong? A: Validation rules and confidence checks are there to stop a doubtful value before it is posted and send the document to a person instead. Corrections are logged and reviewed in weekly tuning, so the cause gets fixed rather than patched. Q: Does it replace our AP or onboarding team? A: It removes the retyping. Your team moves to reviewing exceptions, dealing with suppliers and customers, and approving payments, which is the work that needs judgment."},{"id":"k57","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: Which systems can it post to? A: NetSuite, Dynamics 365, SAP Business One, Xero, QuickBooks Online, Sage Intacct and Salesforce, plus most other ERP, CRM or case systems with an API. If a system has no API, the agent can produce validated import files instead. Q: Is it safe for ID documents and financial data? A: Yes, with the right setup. Data is encrypted, kept in your chosen region, masked in logs and deleted on your schedule, with private-cloud and on-premise options. For KYC, the agent prepares and checks the documents, and decisions about customers stay with your compliance team."},{"id":"k58","title":"Document Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-document-processing-agent/","text":"Q: Which documents and languages does it handle? A: Invoices, receipts, purchase orders, contracts, claim forms, bank statements, IDs, utility bills and logistics documents, in English, Arabic and other major languages. Handwriting and poor scans are harder to read, so they go to review more often."},{"id":"k59","title":"Packaged AI agents: Ops Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Price: From $2,000 + $299/mo. Our Ops Agent is AI workflow automation for the repetitive work between your email, spreadsheets, CRM and ERP. It reads emails and documents, updates records, routes requests and chases follow-ups, built on n8n, Make or custom code, whichever your team can maintain. Anything irreversible waits for human approval, every run is logged, and it goes live in about two weeks."},{"id":"k60","title":"Ops Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Q: How is this different from Zapier or a normal automation? A: Rule-based automations follow fixed steps and break when an input changes shape. The Ops Agent adds AI steps that read unstructured emails and documents, make routing decisions and draft replies, while the plumbing stays in a proven workflow engine. You get the flexibility of AI with the predictability of a workflow. Q: Do you build on n8n, Make or custom code? A: Whichever your team can maintain. n8n suits teams that want to self-host and keep data in their own cloud, Make suits teams that want a visual tool with many ready connectors, and custom code suits high volumes or unusual systems. We recommend one in writing after mapping the process."},{"id":"k61","title":"Ops Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Q: What happens if the AI gets something wrong? A: Every AI step has a confidence threshold, and anything below it goes to a person instead of into your systems. Irreversible actions always wait for approval, and every run is logged, so a mistake can be traced, fixed and rolled back. Q: Can it work with an older ERP that has no modern API? A: Often, yes. We can connect through database views, file drops, email or an existing integration layer. If a system has no safe way in, we tell you during mapping instead of building something fragile."},{"id":"k62","title":"Ops Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-workflow-automation-agent/","text":"Q: Who owns the workflows? A: You do. Workflows live in your own account or your self-hosted n8n, and each one is documented so your team or another provider can maintain it. Q: Which process should we automate first? A: Pick one that is frequent, rule-heavy and has a clear owner. Invoice intake, lead routing and customer onboarding are common first choices. We help you choose on the first call and add more once the first workflow is stable."},{"id":"k63","title":"Packaged AI agents: Data Analyst Agent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Price: From $3,000 + $399/mo. Our Data Analyst Agent is an AI data analyst that answers plain-English questions from your database, warehouse or BI tool. It writes read-only SQL against tables and views you approve, shows the query, a table and a chart, and sends scheduled summaries to Slack, Teams or email. Built for teams without a full-time analyst, it goes live in 2–3 weeks."},{"id":"k64","title":"Data Analyst Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Q: Can the agent change or delete our data? A: No. It connects with a read-only database user and can only see the tables and views you approve. Every query is logged, and limits on rows, time and warehouse cost stop anything heavy. Q: How do we know the answers are right? A: Every answer shows the SQL it ran, so it can be checked. Before launch we test the agent against your own questions with known answers, and we rerun that test after every change. When a term is ambiguous, the agent asks what you mean instead of guessing."},{"id":"k65","title":"Data Analyst Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Q: Do we need a data warehouse first? A: No. It works with a production database, a read replica, a warehouse or the database behind your BI tool. If it has to query production, we point it at a replica or set strict limits so it never slows your app. Q: What data does the AI model see? A: The schema descriptions, your question and the result rows needed to write the answer. Sensitive columns can be masked or excluded, providers are configured not to train on your data, and the model can run in the cloud region you choose."},{"id":"k66","title":"Data Analyst Agent: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-data-analyst-agent/","text":"Q: How is this different from the AI built into Power BI or Looker? A: Built-in assistants work well inside one tool. The Data Analyst Agent works across your databases, uses definitions you approve, lives in Slack or Teams, and sends digests and alerts. If you already use a BI tool, it complements it rather than replacing it. Q: Will it replace our data analyst? A: No. It takes the quick ad hoc questions off your analyst's plate so they can spend time on deeper work. Many teams without an analyst use it to get answers they could not get before."},{"id":"k67","title":"Packaged AI agents: MCP Connector","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Price: From $2,500. Our MCP Connector is an MCP server development service. We build Model Context Protocol servers that let Claude, ChatGPT and Microsoft Copilot read from and act on your internal systems: databases, CRM, ERP, ticketing and documents. Every server ships with least-privilege scopes, OAuth sign-in, rate limits, audit logs and approval for write actions. Delivered in 2–4 weeks as a one-off project."},{"id":"k68","title":"MCP Connector: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Q: What is an MCP server? A: The Model Context Protocol (MCP) is an open standard, introduced by Anthropic and now supported by OpenAI, Microsoft and others, that lets AI apps connect to tools and data in one consistent way. An MCP server is the service that sits in front of your system and exposes a defined set of tools to an AI client. You build it once and use it from any client that supports MCP. Q: Why not just use an open-source MCP server from GitHub? A: Many are fine for personal use, but they often run with one broad token, have no per-user sign-in and keep no audit trail. For company data you need scopes, identity, approval steps and logs. We can harden an existing server or build one designed for your systems."},{"id":"k69","title":"MCP Connector: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Q: Can the AI change data in our systems? A: Only through write tools you approve, and each write pauses for confirmation by the user or a named approver. Everything else is read-only by default, and a kill switch turns any tool off instantly. Q: Which AI clients will it work with? A: Claude (web, desktop and Claude Code), ChatGPT on plans that allow custom connectors, Microsoft Copilot Studio, and coding agents such as Cursor and VS Code. Client support changes quickly, so we test against the clients your team actually uses."},{"id":"k70","title":"MCP Connector: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/mcp-server-development/","text":"Q: Where does the MCP server run? A: In your own cloud on AWS, Azure or Google Cloud, or on-premises behind your gateway. Credentials and data stay in your environment, and only the results of approved tool calls go back to the AI client. Q: Is this a monthly subscription? A: No. The MCP Connector is a one-off project, and you own the code. An optional maintenance plan keeps it updated as the MCP specification, your systems and the AI clients change."},{"id":"k71","title":"Packaged AI agents: Guardrail & Eval Audit","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Price: From $2,500. Our Guardrail & Eval Audit is a fixed-price LLM security audit for AI apps, chatbots and agents. We red-team your system for prompt injection, jailbreaks, data and PII leakage, tool misuse and hallucination, map each finding to the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, and deliver a written report with fixes and a CI eval suite. Report in about two weeks, retest included."},{"id":"k72","title":"Guardrail & Eval Audit: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Q: What is an LLM security audit? A: It is a structured attempt to break your AI app the way a real attacker or a careless user would. We test for prompt injection, jailbreaks, data leakage, tool misuse and hallucination, then report what we found, how serious it is and how to fix it. Q: How is this different from a normal penetration test? A: A penetration test looks at your network, servers and web app. An LLM audit looks at how the model behaves, what it can be talked into, what it retrieves and which tools it can call. The two complement each other, and we can cover both if you need them."},{"id":"k73","title":"Guardrail & Eval Audit: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Q: Which AI apps can you test? A: Chatbots, copilots, RAG search, document tools and agents with tool access, built on OpenAI, Anthropic, Azure OpenAI, AWS Bedrock, Google Vertex AI or open models, with any framework. We need a staging environment or test tenant and accounts for each user role. Q: Will testing affect our customers or production systems? A: No, as long as we test on staging or a test tenant, which is our default. Rules of engagement set the scope and time windows, and anything that could trigger a real action runs against sandboxed tools."},{"id":"k74","title":"Guardrail & Eval Audit: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-security-audit/","text":"Q: Do you fix the issues as well? A: The report gives specific fixes for your architecture, and most teams apply them in-house. If you prefer, we can implement the fixes as a separate piece of work. Either way, the retest of every finding is included. Q: Does the audit make us compliant? A: No single test makes you compliant. The report and eval suite give your compliance team documented evidence of AI risk testing, mapped to the OWASP Top 10 for LLM Applications, which supports frameworks such as the NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001 and the EU AI Act."},{"id":"k75","title":"Packaged AI agents: AI MVP Sprint","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Price: From $12,000. Our AI MVP Sprint is fixed-price AI MVP development for founders and product teams. In 6–8 weeks we take your idea through discovery, a clickable prototype, the build (web app, AI features and evals) and launch, with a demo every week. Fixed scope, fixed price, an NDA from the first call, and you own 100% of the code and IP."},{"id":"k76","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: What can realistically be built in 6–8 weeks? A: One core user journey done properly, with sign-in, an admin area and the AI features that make the product valuable. Discovery is there to cut everything else to a later list. Keeping the first version small is what keeps the date and the price fixed. Q: What if we need to change the scope during the sprint? A: Small changes are swapped in through a short change note, so something of similar size moves to the later list and the date and price hold. A larger change gets a written quote and a new date before any work starts, so there are no surprises."},{"id":"k77","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Do I really own the code and IP? A: Yes, 100%. The code and IP are yours, the handover includes the repository, documentation and deployment access, and you can take the code to any team at any time. We can also set up the repository and cloud accounts in your name from the start if you prefer. Q: Which AI models do you use? A: Whichever fits the job on quality, speed, cost and data rules, usually OpenAI or Anthropic models, or an open model when data must stay in your cloud. We keep the model behind a thin layer and test it with evals, so you can switch later without a rewrite."},{"id":"k78","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Will you sign an NDA before I share my idea? A: Yes. We sign an NDA from the first call, before you share any detail. Your idea, data and documents are only seen by the people working on your sprint. Q: Can you work with my CTO or in-house developers? A: Yes. Your developers can join the repository, review code and attend the weekly demos from the start, which makes the handover much smoother. Many teams use the sprint to get a solid base their own team then grows."},{"id":"k79","title":"AI MVP Sprint: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/ai-agents/ai-mvp-development/","text":"Q: What happens after launch? A: You get 30 days of post-launch support for fixes and small adjustments. After that, you can run the product with your own team, bring us back for the next version, or hire a dedicated team from us."},{"id":"k80","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Receptionist Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/receptionist/","text":"Talk to a real AI voice receptionist for a fictional dental clinic. Use your microphone or type. It answers questions, checks the calendar, books you in, escalates urgent cases and asks staff before it bends a rule. The trace beside the call shows every step and why it took it."},{"id":"k81","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Support Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/support/","text":"Chat with an AI support agent for a fictional online store. It answers from the help center with sources, checks your identity before it touches an order, starts returns and refunds, and asks a person to approve anything over its limit. Every step is in the trace."},{"id":"k82","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): WhatsApp Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/whatsapp/","text":"Chat with a WhatsApp-style AI agent for a fictional Dubai boutique, in English, Arabic or Urdu. It answers from the catalog, shares live order status, recovers an abandoned basket with a checkout link and checks with the manager before a big discount."},{"id":"k83","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Booking Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/booking/","text":"Send a sample enquiry to a fictional remodeling firm and the AI booking agent texts you back within seconds. It asks qualifying questions, books a free estimate on the calendar, schedules reminders and keeps the CRM record up to date, with a person approving anything outside the rules."},{"id":"k84","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): SDR Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/sdr/","text":"Pick a sample company and the AI SDR agent researches it, checks the fit, finds the right person (respecting a do-not-contact list) and drafts a short, specific email that must cite a real buying signal. Nothing goes out until you approve the sequence."},{"id":"k85","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Social Media Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/social/","text":"Brief the AI social media agent for a fictional Manchester pizzeria and it plans a week of Instagram and X posts in the brand voice, checks each one against platform limits and allergy rules, and answers comments. Posts and complaint replies wait for your approval."},{"id":"k86","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): SEO & GEO Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/seo/","text":"The AI SEO & GEO agent audits a fictional bike shop’s pages in code, shows keyword gaps and whether AI assistants cite the business, then drafts titles, descriptions and FAQs that are validated before you approve publishing."},{"id":"k87","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Ads Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/ads/","text":"The AI ads agent reads a sample Meta and Google Ads account, explains ROAS per campaign and proposes budget moves from losers to winners. Hard limits run in code (per-campaign change, total budget), and nothing changes until you approve."},{"id":"k88","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Reputation Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/reputation/","text":"The AI reputation agent drafts on-brand replies to a fictional café’s Google reviews, posts the positive ones, sends critical ones to the owner for approval, reports fake or spam reviews and asks every recent customer for a review, the way Google’s rules require."},{"id":"k89","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Knowledge Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/knowledge/","text":"Ask a fictional company’s policies anything: leave, expenses, travel, IT security. The AI knowledge assistant answers only from its sources, cites each one, says when it does not know, and hides manager-only sections from employees. It is the same RAG pattern we build over your own documents."},{"id":"k90","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Document Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/document/","text":"The AI document agent reads sample supplier invoices, extracts the fields into structured JSON and validates them in code: line maths, VAT, totals, purchase-order match and supplier. Clean small invoices post to the ERP; anything else waits for a person."},{"id":"k91","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Ops Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/ops/","text":"The AI ops agent runs a fictional print shop’s order-to-invoice workflow: it reads the email, matches the customer in the CRM, prices the job from the price list, creates the invoice, logs it, notifies the team and asks you before emailing the customer."},{"id":"k92","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Data Analyst Agent live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/data/","text":"Ask a fictional coffee shop’s database anything: revenue by month, best sellers, customer countries. The AI data analyst writes the SQL, runs it on a real read-only database with personal data masked, and answers with a table and a chart."},{"id":"k93","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): MCP Connector live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/mcp/","text":"An AI assistant answers questions by calling a fictional company’s CRM, support tickets and docs through MCP servers. You see every JSON-RPC call, set the token’s scopes yourself, and approve any write. It is the same pattern we use to connect Claude, ChatGPT or Copilot to your systems."},{"id":"k94","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): Guardrail & Eval Audit live dem","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/guardrail/","text":"A fictional bank’s AI assistant hides a secret code. Try any jailbreak you like. Four layers defend it: input checks with a prompt-injection classifier, hardened instructions, tools that verify in code, and an output filter. The scoreboard shows which layer stopped each attack."},{"id":"k95","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): AI MVP Sprint live demo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/mvp/","text":"Describe your AI product idea and our scoping agent interviews you, cuts it to a launchable MVP of five core features, lays out the build plan and prices it with the same estimator our team uses. A fixed quote follows a call."},{"id":"k96","title":"Live AI agent demos (try them in the browser, no sign-up): All live demos","url":"https://visionbotix.com/demos/","text":"16 agents live on fictional businesses, with every tool call, guardrail and approval shown. A site concierge on every page answers questions about Visionbotix."},{"id":"k97","title":"Services: AI agent development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Price: From $8,000. Visionbotix builds custom AI agents that plan, use your tools and finish multi-step work, such as triaging tickets, reconciling records or preparing reports. Each agent connects to your systems through APIs or MCP, works behind guardrails and human approval gates, and ships with an eval suite and an audit log. Projects are fixed price, and you own the code."},{"id":"k98","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: What is the difference between an AI agent and a chatbot? A: A chatbot answers questions in a conversation. An AI agent takes actions to finish a task. It plans the steps, uses your tools such as the CRM, inbox or database, checks its own work and asks a person for approval when your rules require it. Q: Should we build a custom agent or use a packaged one? A: Start with a packaged agent when the job is common, such as answering calls, booking or support, because it goes live in about two weeks at a lower price. Build a custom agent when the work depends on your own systems, rules or data, or when the agent is part of your product."},{"id":"k99","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: Which models and frameworks do you use? A: We are model-agnostic. We choose between Claude, GPT, Gemini and open models such as Llama for each task based on quality, cost and your data rules, and we build with LangGraph, the OpenAI Agents SDK or plain code where that is simpler. The design lets you switch models later without a rebuild. Q: How do you stop an agent from making costly mistakes? A: Agents only get the tools and data their job needs, risky actions wait at an approval gate, and every step is in the audit log. Before launch the agent must pass an eval suite built from your real cases, and we re-run it after every change."},{"id":"k100","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: Can the agent run on our own infrastructure? A: Yes. We deploy in your AWS, Azure or Google Cloud account, on your own servers, or fully air-gapped with open models when data must never leave your network. Q: How long does it take to build a custom AI agent? A: A focused single-task agent is usually live in six to ten weeks, including a prototype on your real data in the first two to three weeks. Multi-agent systems are planned in milestones, and you see a working demo every week."},{"id":"k101","title":"AI agent development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-agent-development/","text":"Q: Do we own the agent and the code? A: Yes. The contract assigns 100% of the code, prompts, configuration and IP to you on payment, and the repository is yours, so you can run it with or without us."},{"id":"k102","title":"Services: Generative AI development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Price: From $6,000. Visionbotix builds generative AI applications for SaaS companies and data-heavy teams: LLM apps, RAG over company documents, fine-tuned models and AI features inside existing products. Every build ships with an eval suite, guardrails and cost controls, runs on the model that fits your data rules, and is fixed price, with 100% of the code yours."},{"id":"k103","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: What does generative AI development include? A: It means building software around large language models that write, summarize, extract or answer from your data, such as a document Q&A tool, a drafting assistant or an AI feature in your SaaS. It differs from agent development in one way. A generative AI app produces an answer or a draft for a person, while an agent goes on to take actions in your systems. Q: Should we use RAG or fine-tuning? A: Use RAG when answers must come from facts that change and you need sources, such as policies, contracts or product data. Use fine-tuning when you need a fixed format or tone at high volume, or want a smaller model to do one narrow task cheaply. Most projects start with RAG and good prompts, and we fine-tune only when the evals show a gap that prompting cannot close."},{"id":"k104","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: How do you stop the model from making things up? A: We ground answers in your retrieved content, require a citation for every claim and tell the model to say it does not know when the sources are silent. The eval suite measures how often answers stay faithful to the sources, and high-stakes outputs such as legal or medical text go to a person for review before they are used. Q: Will our data be used to train someone else's model? A: No. We use enterprise API terms that exclude your data from training, or deploy open models such as Llama or Mistral in your own cloud or on-premises when data must not leave your environment. Personal data can also be masked before any model sees it."},{"id":"k105","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: Can we switch models later? A: Yes. We put a thin layer between your application and the model provider, so switching is a configuration change followed by an eval run. When a new model is released, we can score it on your own eval set before you decide to move. Q: Can you add generative AI to our existing product? A: Yes. We work in your repository and your stack, ship the feature behind a feature flag, keep each customer's data isolated and add usage limits so one tenant cannot run up the bill. Your engineers review every pull request, and we hand over documentation and the eval suite with the code."},{"id":"k106","title":"Generative AI development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/generative-ai-development/","text":"Q: What happens after launch? A: The first 30 days of fixes and tuning are included. After that you can run it yourself with the eval suite and dashboards we hand over, or take a monthly plan where we watch quality and cost, re-run evals and tune retrieval and prompts as your content changes."},{"id":"k107","title":"Services: AI automation","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Price: From $2,000. Visionbotix is an AI automation agency for operations, finance and sales teams. We automate email triage, data entry, reporting and CRM or ERP sync using n8n, Make, Zapier or custom code, with AI steps for messy inputs and human approval for risky actions. Work is fixed price per workflow or monthly, and every workflow is yours."},{"id":"k108","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: What is the difference between AI automation and regular automation? A: Regular automation follows fixed rules, such as copying two fields from a form into the CRM. AI automation adds steps that understand unstructured input, like reading an email to work out what the customer wants or pulling totals from a scanned invoice. The workflow engine still controls the order of steps and the approvals, so results stay predictable. Q: Should we use n8n, Make, Zapier or custom code? A: Zapier is the quickest for simple flows between popular apps. Make handles visual flows with more branching, n8n suits teams that want to self-host and keep data in their own cloud, and custom code fits high volumes or systems without good connectors. We recommend one per workflow in writing, and many clients end up with a mix."},{"id":"k109","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: Our existing automations keep breaking. Can you fix them? A: Yes. We list what you have, document what each automation does, add error handling and alerts, and remove duplicates that fight each other. Fragile flows are rebuilt in a sturdier tool only where that is worth it. Q: Which processes should we automate first? A: The best first candidates happen every day, follow mostly the same steps and hurt when they are late, such as invoice entry, lead routing or the morning sales report. We rank your candidates during the process review by time saved and risk, and start with one that pays back quickly."},{"id":"k110","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: Will automation replace our staff? A: It replaces the repetitive steps, not the judgment. In most teams people move from typing and checking to handling exceptions, approvals and customers. We design each workflow with the people who do the job today, so it fits how they actually work. Q: Who maintains the workflows after launch? A: Your choice. Workflows live in your own accounts or your self-hosted n8n, with documentation your team can follow. If you would rather not maintain them, a monthly plan covers monitoring, fixes when a connected app changes, and new workflows as you need them."},{"id":"k111","title":"AI automation: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-automation/","text":"Q: Is our data safe in tools like Zapier and Make? A: Both process data in their own cloud, which is fine for many workflows. For sensitive data we use self-hosted n8n or custom code in your environment, mask personal data before any AI step and give each workflow only the access it needs."},{"id":"k112","title":"Services: AI chatbot development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix builds custom AI chatbots for support, sales and internal teams, on websites, help desks, WhatsApp, Instagram and Messenger. Each bot answers from your approved content, speaks English, Arabic, Urdu and other languages, and hands the conversation to a person with full context. Packaged chat agents go live in about two weeks; custom builds are fixed price."},{"id":"k113","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: What is the difference between a rule-based chatbot and an AI chatbot? A: A rule-based chatbot follows buttons, keywords and a fixed decision tree, so it fails when people phrase things their own way. An AI chatbot understands free text, keeps track of the conversation and answers from your content. We still use buttons and fixed flows inside an AI bot where precision matters, such as taking a payment. Q: Do we need a custom chatbot or a packaged chat agent? A: If you need common support or WhatsApp sales jobs on standard tools, our packaged Support Agent or WhatsApp Agent goes live in about two weeks. Choose a custom chatbot when it must work with unusual systems, serve staff rather than customers, live inside your own product or meet strict data rules."},{"id":"k114","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: How do you stop the chatbot from making things up? A: The bot only answers from the content you approve, and when that content does not cover a question it says so and offers a person. Before launch it must pass a test set built from your real conversations, and we review transcripts in the first weeks to close the gaps. Q: Can the chatbot speak Arabic and Urdu? A: Yes. It understands and replies in Arabic, Urdu, English and other major languages, including Roman Urdu and messages that switch language halfway. It answers in the customer's language by default, and we test each language on real phrasing from your market before launch."},{"id":"k115","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: Can it run on WhatsApp and Instagram? A: Yes, through the WhatsApp Business Platform and Meta's messaging APIs. Meta has rules on when a business can message first and which templates it can use, and we build the bot around them. We also help you set up and verify the business account if you do not have one yet. Q: Can a chatbot be used with patient data under HIPAA? A: It can, with the right setup. We deploy on providers that sign a BAA, keep data in your chosen region, encrypt it, limit what the bot can see and log every access. We document the data flow so your compliance lead can review it and sign off."},{"id":"k116","title":"AI chatbot development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-chatbot-development/","text":"Q: What happens when the bot cannot help? A: It hands the conversation to a person in your help desk, shared inbox or WhatsApp team inbox, with the transcript and a one-line summary. Outside working hours it collects contact details and tells the customer when to expect a reply."},{"id":"k117","title":"Services: AI voice agents","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix builds AI voice agents that answer and make phone calls for clinics, service businesses, sales and support teams. They hold natural conversations, book into your calendar, update your CRM, transfer to a person on your rules and tell callers they are speaking to an AI. Packaged receptionists go live in about two weeks; custom voice agents are fixed price."},{"id":"k118","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: What is an AI voice agent? A: It is software that answers or makes phone calls and talks like a person. Speech recognition turns the caller's words into text, a language model decides what to say and do, and a synthetic voice replies, while connections to your calendar and CRM let it book, look up and update records during the call. Q: Do callers have to be told they are talking to an AI? A: We build the disclosure in for every client, whatever the local rules say, because callers trust a clear answer more than a surprise. The greeting says it is an AI assistant, and asking for a person transfers the call or books a callback."},{"id":"k119","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: Can it make outbound calls? A: Yes, for reminders, confirmations, lead follow-up and qualification. In many countries, including the US and UK, automated or AI-voiced calls need prior consent and must respect calling hours and do-not-call lists. We build consent checks, calling windows and opt-outs into every campaign, but your legal team should confirm the rules for each market you call. Q: How natural does it sound? A: Close to a person on a good line. We pick a voice from ElevenLabs or another provider, tune how quickly it responds and let it handle interruptions and pauses. You hear recorded test calls before go-live and can change the voice or wording at any point."},{"id":"k120","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: Can it work with our existing phone system? A: Yes. You can forward your current number, use a new Twilio number or connect a SIP trunk to your PBX or contact center platform. The agent can transfer calls to extensions, queues or mobile numbers based on your rules. Q: Can it handle callers in different languages? A: Yes. The agent greets callers in your main language and switches when the caller does, across English, Arabic, Urdu and other major languages. We choose a voice per language and test each one with the phrasing and accents your callers actually use."},{"id":"k121","title":"AI voice agents: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-voice-agents/","text":"Q: Are call recordings stored safely? A: Recording is optional and announced when it is on. Recordings and transcripts are encrypted, stored in the region you choose and deleted on your schedule, and for US healthcare we deploy on providers that sign a BAA."},{"id":"k122","title":"Services: AI consulting","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Price: From $490. Visionbotix offers AI consulting services for business leaders who want a clear AI plan. We start with a 1-week AI Opportunity Audit: we map your workflows, rank AI use cases by value and risk, check data readiness and recommend build, buy or wait in a written plan. The audit fee is credited in full against a build within 60 days."},{"id":"k123","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: What does an AI consultant actually do? A: An AI consultant helps you decide where AI pays off and how to adopt it safely. That means mapping your workflows, ranking use cases, choosing between tools and custom builds, checking your data and setting rules for how staff use AI. Because we also build AI systems, our advice is grounded in what is practical to ship. Q: What is the AI Opportunity Audit? A: It is a fixed-scope, one-week engagement. We interview your team, map where AI could help, test the best ideas on your data and hand over a written plan with ranked use cases, build-vs-buy advice and governance steps. If you start a build with us within 60 days, the audit fee is credited in full."},{"id":"k124","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: Do we have to build with you after the audit? A: No. The plan is yours to use with your own team, another vendor or an off-the-shelf tool. We write it so anyone can act on it, and the credit simply applies if you choose us within 60 days. Q: Is our data ready for AI? A: Often more than you think, because many useful projects start with documents, emails and tickets you already have. The data readiness review shows, per use case, what exists, what is missing or messy, and whether you are allowed to use it, so you know what to fix first."},{"id":"k125","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: Do you help with AI governance and the EU AI Act? A: Yes. We draft an AI use policy, build a register of the AI systems you use, map each to its likely risk tier and set approval and human-oversight steps. This is practical awareness, not legal advice, and we flag where your counsel should review. Q: Should we build our own AI or buy a tool? A: Buy when the job is common and a vendor already does it well on acceptable data terms. Build when the work depends on your own process, systems or data, or when AI is part of what you sell. Most companies end up with a mix, and the audit says which applies to each use case."},{"id":"k126","title":"AI consulting: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ai-consulting/","text":"Q: Can you train our team to use AI? A: Yes. We run practical workshops for leaders and staff built around their own tasks, covering safe use of AI tools, good prompting and how to spot work worth automating. Training can sit alongside your new AI use policy so people know what is allowed."},{"id":"k127","title":"Services: Custom software development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Price: From $5,000. Visionbotix builds custom software for businesses that have outgrown spreadsheets and off-the-shelf tools: internal tools, customer portals, ERP and CRM extensions, integrations and APIs, and modernized legacy systems. We can take over an existing codebase, add AI features where they save real time, and demo progress weekly. Projects are fixed price by milestone, and you own the code."},{"id":"k128","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: What is custom software development? A: It is software designed and built for your own processes, users and data, instead of a product you rent and adapt to. You decide what it does, it connects to the systems you already use, and you own the code outright. Q: Should we buy off-the-shelf software or build custom? A: Buy when a mainstream product fits most of your process and the gap is minor. Build when the gap is the part that makes your business different, when you are paying for several tools to fake one workflow, or when the tool cannot connect to your other systems. Often the right answer is both, with a custom layer on top of what you already own."},{"id":"k129","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: Can you take over a codebase another team built? A: Yes. We start with a short audit of the code, infrastructure and documentation, tell you plainly what is sound and what is risky, and then fix the urgent issues and keep shipping. You get a written report either way. Q: How do you modernize a legacy system without stopping the business? A: We replace it in slices. The new system runs alongside the old one, data syncs between them, and each module moves over only after it is tested against real records. Your team keeps working throughout, and there is always a way back until cutover."},{"id":"k130","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: Can you integrate with our ERP, CRM or accounting software? A: Usually, yes. If the system has an API, webhooks or a database we can reach, we can integrate with it. We check access and limits during discovery, before you commit to a fixed price. Q: How long does a custom software project take? A: A focused first release, such as an internal tool or a portal, is usually live in 8–14 weeks. Larger systems are planned in milestones that each deliver something your team can use, and you see a working demo every week."},{"id":"k131","title":"Custom software development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/custom-software-development/","text":"Q: Do we own the software and the code? A: Yes. The contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you on payment, the repository lives in your account, and the documentation is written so any competent team can maintain it, with or without us."},{"id":"k132","title":"Services: Web app development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Price: From $3,000. Visionbotix designs and builds web apps for startups and growing businesses: dashboards, customer portals, marketplaces, e-commerce stores, progressive web apps and marketing sites. We use React, Next.js, Astro and Node or Laravel, and build for speed, accessibility and search from day one. You see a working demo every week, pay by milestone, and own the code."},{"id":"k133","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: What is the difference between a website and a web app? A: A website mostly shows information, such as pages about your company or products. A web app lets people do things, such as log in, order, book, upload or manage data. Many projects are both, and we build them on one stack so the marketing pages and the product share a design and a domain. Q: Which framework will you use? A: We choose for your product, not for habit. Next.js or Astro suit sites where search matters, React, Angular or Vue suit complex logged-in apps, and Node, NestJS or Laravel sit behind them. We explain the choice in the scope, and every option is mainstream enough that any good developer can pick it up."},{"id":"k134","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: Will the new site be good for SEO and AI search? A: Yes, we build for it from the start. Pages are fast, rendered on the server or pre-built, marked up with structured data and written so each page answers one question clearly. When you relaunch, we map and redirect old URLs so existing rankings carry over. Q: Should we build a progressive web app or a native mobile app? A: A progressive web app is a good first step when your users mainly need forms, browsing and notifications, because one codebase covers every device and there is no app store review. Choose a native or cross-platform app when you need deep device features, offline-heavy use or a store presence. We can start with a PWA and add mobile apps later on the same back end."},{"id":"k135","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: Can you redesign or rebuild our existing site without losing traffic? A: Yes. We audit what ranks and converts today, keep or improve those pages, set up redirects for every URL that changes and check search console after launch. Content and data move across before the switch, not after. Q: Can our team update content without a developer? A: Yes. We connect a headless CMS or an admin panel for pages, blog posts, products and media, with roles so editors cannot break the layout. We show your team how to use it before launch."},{"id":"k136","title":"Web app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/web-app-development/","text":"Q: Who hosts the web app after launch? A: You choose. We deploy to your own Vercel, AWS, Google Cloud or Azure account, so the hosting bills and access are yours. We can keep it running for you on a monthly plan, or hand it over to your team."},{"id":"k137","title":"Services: Mobile app development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Price: From $8,000. Visionbotix builds iOS and Android apps for startups and businesses, in native Swift and Kotlin or cross-platform with React Native or Flutter. We handle design, offline mode, push, payments, AI features, the back end and store submission. Apps built by our team are live on the App Store and Google Play. Fixed price by milestone, and you own the code."},{"id":"k138","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Do we need separate apps for iOS and Android? A: Usually not. React Native and Flutter let one team ship both from a single codebase, which keeps features in step and lowers the cost of every change. Native Swift and Kotlin make sense when the app leans hard on device features, heavy graphics or the latest platform APIs. Q: React Native or Flutter, which should we choose? A: Both are mature and both reach iOS and Android. React Native is the natural pick if you have a React web app or a JavaScript team, because code and skills carry over. Flutter suits highly custom, brand-led interfaces that must look identical on every phone. We recommend one in the scope and explain why."},{"id":"k139","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Will you publish the app to the App Store and Google Play? A: Yes. We prepare the listings, screenshots, privacy labels and review notes, submit the builds and handle any reviewer questions. Store approval is Apple's and Google's decision, so we design to their guidelines from the start to avoid surprises. Q: Can the app work offline? A: Yes, when the product needs it. We store data on the device, queue changes while there is no signal and sync them safely when the connection returns, with clear rules for conflicts."},{"id":"k140","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Can you add AI features to a mobile app? A: Yes. Common examples are document and photo scanning, voice input, translation, smart search and in-app assistants. Some run on the device for speed and privacy, others call a model in the cloud, and we set cost limits and guardrails either way. Q: Can you take over or fix an app another developer built? A: Yes. We review the code, dependencies, crash reports and store status, tell you plainly what to keep and what to rebuild, and then fix the urgent issues first. You get a written report before you commit to anything larger."},{"id":"k141","title":"Mobile app development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/mobile-app-development/","text":"Q: Who owns the app, the code and the store listings? A: You do. The App Store and Google Play accounts, signing keys and repository are set up in your name, and the contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you on payment."},{"id":"k142","title":"Services: SaaS and MVP development","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Price: From $12,000. Visionbotix builds SaaS products and MVPs for founders and product teams. We scope the smallest launchable version, then build it with sign-in, roles, Stripe billing, an admin panel, analytics and AI features, on a multi-tenant base that can scale. You get a demo every week, a fixed price per milestone, an NDA from the first call, and all the code."},{"id":"k143","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: What is an MVP, and what should ours include? A: An MVP is the smallest version of your product that real users can use and pay for, so you learn what works before building more. Ours usually include one core journey done well, sign-in, basic admin and, for SaaS, billing. Everything else goes on a later list that real usage will reorder. Q: How is this different from your AI MVP Sprint? A: The AI MVP Sprint is a packaged, fixed-scope offer that takes an AI-native idea to a working product in 6–8 weeks. This service covers any SaaS or MVP, with or without AI, and the path after launch, such as multi-tenant scale, larger billing models and enterprise features."},{"id":"k144","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Will we have to rebuild the MVP later? A: Not if it is built right. We cut features, not foundations, so the MVP already has a clean data model, tenant separation, tests and mainstream frameworks. Growing it means adding modules, not starting again. Q: We are non-technical founders. Can you still work with us? A: Yes. You do not need to know the technology to make good product decisions. You get one named lead who explains choices in plain words, a weekly demo you can click through, and a written scope so you always know what is being built and why."},{"id":"k145","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Can you add AI features to our SaaS? A: Yes. Common examples are assistants that know a customer's own data, document extraction, smart search, summaries and agents that complete tasks. We keep each customer's data separate, set usage limits per account and test the features against real cases before launch. Q: What happens after the MVP launches? A: You get 30 days of support for fixes and tuning. After that you can continue with us on a monthly plan or a dedicated team, or take the code to your own developers, since you own the repository and the documentation."},{"id":"k146","title":"SaaS and MVP development: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/saas-mvp-development/","text":"Q: Do we own the code and the IP? A: Yes. The contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you on payment, and the repository, cloud accounts and Stripe account are in your name from day one, which matters when you raise money."},{"id":"k147","title":"Services: UI/UX design","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix offers UI/UX design for web apps, mobile apps and SaaS products: discovery, UX research, wireframes, clickable Figma prototypes, design systems and accessible interfaces to WCAG AA. We also design AI features so users can see what an agent did and approve it. Start with a design sprint for one product flow, then build it with us or any developer."},{"id":"k148","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: What is the difference between UI and UX design? A: UX design is how the product works, such as the steps a user takes, what they see first and how they recover from mistakes. UI design is how it looks, such as layout, type, color and components. You need both, and we do both in one team. Q: What is a design sprint for one product flow? A: It is a short, fixed-scope engagement that takes one important journey, such as onboarding, checkout or an AI approval flow, from research to a tested, clickable prototype. It is the fastest way to fix a weak flow or to see how we work before a larger project."},{"id":"k149","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: Do you only design, or can you build it too? A: Both. You can take the Figma files and the component library to your own developers, or we can build the product with our web and mobile teams, so nothing is lost between design and code. Q: Can you redesign our product without confusing existing users? A: Yes. We find the screens that cause the most friction, redesign those first and roll changes out in stages, often behind a toggle for early users. Familiar patterns stay where they work."},{"id":"k150","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: How do you design for AI features and agents? A: We make the AI's work visible. Users see what the agent is doing, which sources it used and what it plans to change, and anything risky waits for their approval. We also design how users correct the AI, because trust comes from being able to undo. Q: Will the design be accessible? A: Yes. We design to WCAG AA by default, covering contrast, focus states, keyboard paths, touch target sizes and screen reader labels, and we note these in the handoff so they survive the build."},{"id":"k151","title":"UI/UX design: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/ui-ux-design/","text":"Q: Do we own the design files? A: Yes. The Figma files, components, icons made for you and all design IP are yours on payment, in your own Figma workspace if you prefer."},{"id":"k152","title":"Services: Cloud and DevOps","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Price: From $1,500. Visionbotix sets up and runs cloud infrastructure on AWS, Azure, Google Cloud and Vercel. We build CI/CD pipelines, write the infrastructure as code in Terraform, containerize apps with Docker and Kubernetes, add monitoring and review your cloud bill. We also host private open models on GPUs for AI workloads. Fixed price, and you own every line."},{"id":"k153","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: What do cloud and DevOps services include? A: They cover how your software is hosted, built, released and watched in production. In practice that means a cloud architecture, a CI/CD pipeline, infrastructure as code, containers, monitoring and alerts, and regular cost reviews. You can take one piece, such as a pipeline, or the whole setup. Q: Which cloud should we use? A: It depends on your team, your customers and your data rules more than on features. Vercel or a similar managed platform suits most web products early on, AWS, Azure and Google Cloud suit larger or regulated workloads, and some enterprise buyers require a specific one. We recommend one in writing after the first review."},{"id":"k154","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: Do we really need Kubernetes? A: Often not. Kubernetes pays off when you run many services, need fine control over scaling or must run the same stack across clouds and on-premises. For a single app or a small team, a managed platform or containers on simpler cloud services cost less to run and are easier to hire for. Q: Can you reduce our cloud bill? A: Usually, yes. We review every line of the bill, remove idle resources, right-size servers and databases, and move steady workloads to reserved or committed pricing. You get a ranked list of changes with the effort each one takes, and we make the ones you approve."},{"id":"k155","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: Can you host an open-source LLM privately for us? A: Yes. We deploy open models such as Llama, Mistral or DeepSeek on GPU servers in your cloud account or on your own hardware, with an API your apps can call, access controls and usage monitoring. Prompts and data stay inside your network. Q: Will we be locked in to you? A: No. Everything is written as Terraform and pipeline code in your repository, in your cloud accounts, with runbooks your team can follow. You own 100% of the code and IP, and you can run it with or without us."},{"id":"k156","title":"Cloud and DevOps: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cloud-devops/","text":"Q: Do you offer ongoing DevOps support? A: Yes. After 30 days of included support you can move to a monthly plan in which we watch alerts, apply updates, review costs and handle changes. Or we train your team and step back."},{"id":"k157","title":"Services: Dedicated teams","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Price: From $2,200/mo. Visionbotix gives you full-time AI and ML engineers, full-stack and mobile developers, UI/UX designers and QA engineers who work only on your product. They join your Slack, Jira and GitHub, follow your sprints, overlap your working hours and report through one named lead. You scale the team up or down as the roadmap changes, and you own all the code."},{"id":"k158","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: What is a dedicated development team? A: It is a group of full-time engineers and designers who work only on your product, inside your tools and sprints. You set the priorities day to day, and we handle hiring, payroll, equipment and management through one named lead. Q: How is this different from hiring freelancers? A: Freelancers usually split their time across clients and leave when the contract ends. Our engineers are full time on your product, work as one team, and are backed by a company that stays responsible for delivery and continuity."},{"id":"k159","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: Which time zones do you cover? A: Our engineers work hours that overlap the US, UK, Europe, the Gulf and Australia. We agree the overlap window for each role before the team starts, so standups and reviews happen live. Q: Can we interview the developers first? A: Yes. We propose engineers who match the brief, you interview them, and only the people you approve join your team."},{"id":"k160","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: Can we scale the team up or down? A: Yes. You can add roles as the roadmap grows or reduce the team when a phase ends, with the notice period agreed in the contract. The named lead keeps knowledge in your repository and docs, so changes do not set the work back. Q: Who owns the code and IP? A: You do. The contract assigns 100% of the code and IP to you, all work happens in your repository, and we sign an NDA on request before you share anything."},{"id":"k161","title":"Dedicated teams: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/dedicated-teams/","text":"Q: Can a dedicated team build AI features? A: Yes. Our AI and ML engineers build agents, RAG systems, evals and model integrations with Claude, GPT, Gemini and open models, and they work alongside your existing developers so the skills stay with your team."},{"id":"k162","title":"Services: Computer vision","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Price: From $10,000. Visionbotix builds custom computer vision systems that detect objects, inspect products for defects, read text, recognize authorized people and count footfall. We train models on your own images and run them on your cameras, on edge devices such as NVIDIA Jetson and Raspberry Pi, or in your cloud. Prototypes are fixed price, and you own the model and code."},{"id":"k163","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: What can computer vision do for my business? A: It turns camera images into decisions or data. Common uses are spotting defective parts on a line, reading labels and meters, controlling entry, counting people or stock, and flagging safety risks. If a person can see it consistently in an image, a model can usually be trained to see it too. Q: How many images do we need to train a model? A: It depends on how varied your product and conditions are. Many projects start with a few hundred labeled images per class and grow from there, and we tell you after the first week whether your data is enough. We can also help you capture and label it."},{"id":"k164","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: Can the system run without the cloud? A: Yes. We deploy models on edge devices such as NVIDIA Jetson, Raspberry Pi or an industrial PC next to the camera, so images are processed on site and the system keeps working offline. Only alerts or counts need to leave the device, if anything does. Q: Can you use our existing cameras? A: Often, yes. Most IP cameras that provide a standard video stream work. If the resolution, angle or lighting is not good enough for the task, we recommend specific changes before training starts rather than after."},{"id":"k165","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: How do you handle privacy for face recognition? A: We build face recognition only where people have consented, with a clear enrollment step, encrypted storage of face templates and retention rules you approve. For counting and occupancy we use detection without identity, so nobody is recognized. Q: How accurate will the model be? A: We agree the target with you before training, measure it on images the model has never seen, and report the results honestly. Accuracy depends on your data and conditions, so the pilot on real cameras is where we prove it before a full rollout."},{"id":"k166","title":"Computer vision: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/computer-vision/","text":"Q: Do you have your own vision products? A: Yes. We built and run Smart Livestock, an AI platform for dairy and livestock farms, and Vision AI cameras. The same team builds custom vision systems for clients."},{"id":"k167","title":"Services: IoT and embedded","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Price: From $10,000. Visionbotix designs and builds connected devices end to end: sensor networks, firmware, embedded Linux, FPGA logic, edge AI and ROS robots, connected over MQTT, LoRa, BLE or cellular to dashboards that manage the whole fleet. We take you from a working prototype to a field pilot in milestones at a fixed price, and you own the designs and code."},{"id":"k168","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: What do IoT development services cover? A: Everything needed to put a connected device in the field. That includes choosing sensors and boards, writing the firmware, setting up connectivity, building the backend that stores the data and the dashboard or app people use. We can take on the whole system or one layer of it. Q: Can you take us from an idea to a working prototype? A: Yes. We start with a short feasibility phase to choose components and test the riskiest assumptions, then build a working bench prototype with firmware, data and a first dashboard. A field pilot follows once the prototype proves the idea."},{"id":"k169","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: Which connectivity should we use? A: It depends on range, power and how much data each device sends. LoRa suits small readings over long distances on battery, BLE suits short range and phones, Wi-Fi suits buildings with power, and cellular suits mobile or remote assets. MQTT usually carries the messages once the link is chosen. Q: Do you design FPGA logic? A: Yes. We design FPGA logic for high-speed processing, encryption and real-time control, and our own VX-1 IP Encryptor runs its encryption entirely in FPGA hardware. FPGA work suits problems where software on a processor is too slow or too exposed."},{"id":"k170","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: Can the devices run AI on the edge? A: Yes. We run vision and anomaly-detection models on NVIDIA Jetson, Raspberry Pi and capable microcontrollers, so decisions happen next to the sensor and the device keeps working when the network drops. Q: Do you manufacture the hardware? A: We design and build prototypes and pilot batches, and we prepare the designs and documentation for a manufacturer of your choice to produce at volume. We can stay involved for testing and firmware updates during that handover."},{"id":"k171","title":"IoT and embedded: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/iot-embedded/","text":"Q: How long does a hardware project take? A: A working prototype usually takes six to ten weeks and a field pilot three to six months, depending on how custom the hardware is. Hardware takes longer than software because parts, enclosures and field testing add steps, so we plan it in milestones you can see."},{"id":"k172","title":"Services: Cybersecurity","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Price: From $2,500. Visionbotix secures AI systems and sensitive networks. We red-team LLM apps and agents for prompt injection, data leakage and tool misuse, review the architecture of the software we build, and make our own security products: the VX-1 hardware IP encryptor, ThreatIQ for air-gapped networks and a Cyber Range for team training and device testing. NDA on request from the first call."},{"id":"k173","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: What cybersecurity services do you offer? A: We focus on two areas. For AI systems, we red-team LLM apps and agents and review the architecture of the software we build. For sensitive networks, we offer our own products, the VX-1 IP Encryptor, ThreatIQ and the Cyber Range, which are deployed and supported by our team. Q: What is LLM red teaming? A: It is a structured attempt to make your AI app misbehave the way a real attacker would. We try to override its instructions, extract its system prompt, reach other users' data and misuse the tools it can call, then document what worked and how to fix it."},{"id":"k174","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: Does this replace a traditional penetration test? A: No. A traditional pen test covers your network, servers and web application. LLM red teaming covers the AI layer that those tests were not designed for, such as prompt injection and tool misuse. Most products with AI features need both. Q: Can you secure an AI agent that has access to our systems? A: Yes. We review every tool the agent can call, cut its permissions to what the job needs, add approval steps for risky actions and test whether it can be talked into misusing them. We can also build a secure MCP server so the agent reaches your systems through one controlled gateway."},{"id":"k175","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: What is the VX-1 IP Encryptor? A: It is our hardware network encryptor. It encrypts IP traffic between sites with AES-256 in counter mode on dedicated FPGA hardware, with no operating system to attack. It works transparently on Layer 2 and Layer 3 links, including satellite connections, and its output was checked against the NIST FIPS 197 reference vectors. Q: How does ThreatIQ protect an air-gapped network? A: ThreatIQ runs as a dedicated appliance inside the isolated network with lightweight clients on each endpoint. It assesses vulnerabilities across malware, software, operating systems, web apps, network traffic and services, watches for unusual insider behavior and benchmarks configurations against recognized hardening baselines such as the CIS Benchmarks, all without an internet connection."},{"id":"k176","title":"Cybersecurity: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/services/cybersecurity/","text":"Q: Who is the Cyber Range for? A: It is for security teams that need to practice attack and defense safely, and for organizations that want to test network and security devices before buying them. It runs red team and blue team exercises on realistic simulated traffic and benchmarks devices against standards such as RFC 2544 and RFC 3511, with training for your operators. Q: Is our information kept confidential? A: Yes. We sign an NDA on request before the first technical conversation, test in environments you approve and share findings only with the people you name. Our security products are built for defense, government and enterprise environments where discretion is the norm."},{"id":"k177","title":"Our own products: Wakeel","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Wakeel is an AI legal matching platform built and run by Visionbotix. A person describes a legal problem in their own words, in Urdu, English or Roman Urdu, by typing or speaking. The AI works out the city, case type, court level and budget, then shows verified advocates who fit, with a plain explanation of why each one was matched. Live at https://www.wakeel.com.pk"},{"id":"k178","title":"Wakeel: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Q: What is Wakeel? A: Wakeel is an AI legal matching platform for Pakistan, built and operated by Visionbotix. People describe a legal problem in Urdu, English or Roman Urdu, and the AI matches them with verified advocates who fit their city, case type, court level and budget. Q: Does Wakeel give legal advice? A: No. Wakeel is a referral and matching platform. It helps people find a suitable, verified advocate; the advice comes from the advocate."},{"id":"k179","title":"Wakeel: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Q: How does the AI understand Roman Urdu? A: The AI is built for the way people in Pakistan actually write, including Roman Urdu and mixed Urdu and English. It extracts structured fields (city, practice area, court level, budget) from whatever the person writes or says, and those fields drive the search. Q: How are lawyers verified? A: Before a profile is listed, Wakeel checks active Bar Council enrollment, the advocate's disciplinary history, and their identity and office address."},{"id":"k180","title":"Wakeel: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/wakeel/","text":"Q: What does Wakeel show about Visionbotix? A: It is our own product, built end to end by our team. It shows how we build AI-first interfaces where one plain-language prompt replaces forms and filters, which is the same approach we use for client marketplaces, booking tools and support products. Q: Can you build a prompt-first product like this for my business? A: Yes. We build the prompt interface, the extraction and matching logic, the data model behind it and the admin tools, as a web or mobile app. Book a call and we will scope it, usually with a fixed quote within 24 hours."},{"id":"k181","title":"Our own products: VX-1 IP Encryptor","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"The VX-1 IP Encryptor is a hardware network encryptor from Visionbotix. It encrypts all IP traffic crossing your WAN with AES-256 in counter mode on dedicated FPGA silicon, with no operating system to attack. Place one unit at each end of a link and power on: it works transparently on Layer 2 and Layer 3 networks, including satellite links."},{"id":"k182","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: What is the VX-1 IP Encryptor? A: It is a hardware network encryptor built by Visionbotix on dedicated FPGA silicon. It encrypts all IP traffic crossing a WAN with AES-256 in counter mode at near line-rate speed, deploys plug-and-play with zero configuration and has no operating system, which keeps its attack surface minimal. Q: How is the VX-1 deployed? A: You place one unit at each end of the link, connect it and power it on. It operates transparently at the IP layer, so your routers, switches and endpoints keep their current configuration."},{"id":"k183","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: What networks does the VX-1 work on? A: It works on Layer 2 and Layer 3 networks, including ISP links, private WANs and satellite connections. It has been tested with multi-vendor routing and switching equipment in the path, across VLAN, hybrid and enterprise topologies. Q: Does the VX-1 run software that needs patching? A: No. It has no operating system, no background services and no software stack. Encryption runs entirely in FPGA hardware, which removes the patching, updates and configuration drift that software encryptors need."},{"id":"k184","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: How is the VX-1 different from a software VPN? A: A software VPN runs on an operating system that needs patching and can be attacked. The VX-1 encrypts in FPGA hardware with no operating system, needs no configuration and keeps near line-rate throughput with low latency. Q: How was the encryption validated? A: The AES-256 output was checked byte for byte against the NIST FIPS 197 reference vectors. Performance was measured with the RFC 2544 and ITU-T Y.1564 test suites, and real web, DNS, FTP, SMTP, VoIP and video traffic was verified to pass uninterrupted."},{"id":"k185","title":"VX-1 IP Encryptor: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/vx-1-ip-encryptor/","text":"Q: How much does the VX-1 cost? A: The VX-1 is quoted per deployment, based on the number of links and sites. Ask for a technical briefing and we will prepare a quote for your network."},{"id":"k186","title":"Our own products: ThreatIQ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"ThreatIQ is an internal defense layer for air-gapped and classified networks. One dedicated appliance with lightweight endpoint clients assesses vulnerabilities across six technology layers, detects insider threats with user behavior analytics and benchmarks configurations against the CIS Benchmarks. Everything runs offline, inside the air gap, and nothing leaves the network."},{"id":"k187","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: What is ThreatIQ? A: ThreatIQ is an internal defense platform by Visionbotix for air-gapped and classified networks. It combines vulnerability assessment across six technology layers, user behavior analytics for insider threat detection and compliance benchmarking against the CIS Benchmarks in one appliance. Q: Does ThreatIQ need an internet connection? A: No. ThreatIQ is built offline-first. It runs as a dedicated hardware appliance inside the protected LAN with lightweight clients on each endpoint, and all scanning, analytics and reporting happen inside the air gap. Nothing leaves the network."},{"id":"k188","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: What does ThreatIQ assess? A: Six layers, each assessed independently. These are malware exposure, third-party and custom software, operating systems, web applications against the OWASP Top 10, malicious network traffic, and services and ports following NIST SP 800-115. The results are combined into one report with prioritized remediation. Q: How does ThreatIQ detect insider threats? A: Lightweight endpoint clients monitor user activity across eight behavioral criteria, matched against over 1,000 specific event patterns. Unusual or malicious activity is flagged early so your security team can respond before it escalates."},{"id":"k189","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: Does ThreatIQ work on segmented networks? A: Yes. It supports segmented architectures, including networks split into two lines by a physical or logical air gap. Q: Does ThreatIQ integrate with our existing tools? A: ThreatIQ is self-contained, so the appliance and its endpoint clients are all it needs to run. If you want it to work alongside tools you already use, we scope that during the technical briefing."},{"id":"k190","title":"ThreatIQ: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/threatiq/","text":"Q: How is ThreatIQ priced? A: ThreatIQ is quoted per deployment, based on the size and layout of your network. Ask for a briefing or a demo and we will prepare a quote."},{"id":"k191","title":"Our own products: Cyber Range","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"The Visionbotix Cyber Range is a training and testing platform for security teams. Red and blue teams practice attack and defense on realistic simulated internet traffic, and switches, routers, firewalls and IDS/IPS are benchmarked against standards such as RFC 2544 and RFC 3511 before you buy. We design the range, deliver it and train your operators."},{"id":"k192","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: What is a cyber range? A: A cyber range is to IT security what a firing range is to marksmanship. It is a safe, realistic environment where security teams practice attack and defense, and where network devices are tested before they are deployed. Q: What can be tested on the Visionbotix Cyber Range? A: Switches and routers per RFC 2544 and RFC 2889, firewalls and next-generation firewalls per RFC 3511 and the BMWG methodology, Layer 4 to 7 applications, application servers, IDS/IPS, DLP and antimalware systems. Tests run on realistic simulated internet traffic, attack libraries and traffic replayed from your own applications."},{"id":"k193","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: How do red team and blue team exercises work? A: A red team equipped with professional penetration testing and vulnerability scanning tools attacks infrastructure that a blue team defends with firewalls, IDS/IPS and SIEM. Attacks use real vulnerabilities such as DDoS and SQL injection on simulated traffic, so nothing real is harmed. Q: Does the Cyber Range include training? A: Yes. We deliver customized training on network design, performance testing, attack theory and firewall and IPS deployment, plus dedicated ongoing support. Schedules and plans are agreed with each customer."},{"id":"k194","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: Is the traffic on the range real internet traffic? A: It is simulated, but built to be indistinguishable from the real thing. The range generates business, streaming, gaming, social and peer-to-peer traffic from IANA-allocated address space, with any country selectable as source or target, so teams train on realistic conditions while nothing real is harmed. Q: Can we get reports or connect the range to our own tools? A: Yes. The range produces PDF, Word and HTML reports with graphs and charts, and offers a RESTful API for custom integrations and automation."},{"id":"k195","title":"Cyber Range: questions","url":"https://visionbotix.com/products/cyber-range/","text":"Q: How is the Cyber Range priced? A: Each range is quoted per deployment, based on the teams you train, the devices you test and the training you need. Ask for a briefing and we will prepare a proposal."},{"id":"k196","title":"Our own products","url":"https://visionbotix.com/","text":"- [Smart Livestock](https://livestock.visionbotix.com) - [Vision AI cameras](https://cv.visionbotix.com)"},{"id":"k197","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Genetic sample colle","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/genetic-sample-collection-platform/","text":"A genetics research programme studying inherited disorders. We built a complete sample-management platform for a genetics research programme: an offline-first iPhone and iPad app for questionnaires, pedigree building, document scans and geotagging, plus a companion app that records 3D facial models with Apple's TrueDepth camera, all linked to one family record and synced to a central back office."},{"id":"k198","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Multi-vendor marketp","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/multi-vendor-marketplace-platform/","text":"A multi-vendor marketplace operator. We built a full multi-vendor marketplace: an installable web storefront, customer and rider mobile apps, vendor dashboards, a point-of-sale app and an admin console, all on one inventory. AI tools speed up listing and discovery, and the platform runs in three languages with right-to-left support, designed for low-cost phones."},{"id":"k199","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Touch-free consultat","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/gesture-controlled-consultation-kiosk/","text":"A hair and skin treatment clinic. We built a touch-free consultation kiosk for a hair and skin clinic: a standalone desktop app that runs an interactive quiz and is controlled entirely by hand gestures. Webcam-based computer vision tracks the visitor's hand and turns it into pointer movement, clicks and scrolling, with no touch, keyboard or mouse."},{"id":"k200","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI patient-intake an","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-patient-triage-assistant-clinic-network/","text":"A telehealth clinic network. An AI intake and triage assistant for a telehealth clinic network. Patients describe their symptoms, an LLM pipeline built with LangChain asks adaptive follow-up questions, classifies urgency and the likely department, and gives doctors a ranked summary on a dashboard with history, flags and exportable reports."},{"id":"k201","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Edge AI visual inspe","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/edge-ai-manufacturing-defect-detection/","text":"An industrial parts manufacturer. A real-time visual inspection system for an industrial parts manufacturer. A computer-vision model trained on the factory's own images runs on a Raspberry Pi with a camera at the line, flags defective parts as they pass, alerts supervisors and keeps an inspection log with images. No cloud is involved."},{"id":"k202","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): No-code chatbot buil","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/whatsapp-web-chatbot-builder-platform/","text":"A customer-support software business. A no-code chatbot builder sold as SaaS. Users design FAQ, lead-capture and ticketing bots in a drag-and-drop flow editor, publish them to WhatsApp through Twilio or to a website widget, and track every conversation in an analytics dashboard. Flows can be exported and imported between accounts."},{"id":"k203","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI smart dairy farm ","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-smart-dairy-farm/","text":"Our own product for dairy and livestock farms. Our Smart Livestock product turns a dairy farm into a data-driven operation. Computer vision and IoT sensors record every animal's weight, temperature, milk production, fat content and feed each day, and a dashboard flags health and yield problems early, so farmers act before small issues become expensive."},{"id":"k204","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Field workforce atte","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/field-workforce-attendance-app/","text":"A municipal waste-management company. We built an attendance and location app for a waste-management company whose staff mostly work in the field. Employees mark attendance on their phones, the app logs location in the background every hour, and supervisors see in one view who is in the office, who is on route, and the full history."},{"id":"k205","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI monitoring and at","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/campus-monitoring-robots/","text":"A client running campuses, offices and public-sector facilities. We built two computer-vision robots for campuses and public spaces. The monitoring robot detects smoking, fire, crowding and missing masks and sends alerts with photo evidence. The attendance robot recognises people at the entrance and records attendance and body temperature without contact."},{"id":"k206","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Contactless temperat","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/contactless-temperature-screening/","text":"A client with offices, factories and retail sites. We built an autonomous temperature-screening station: it detects each person's face, measures body temperature without contact, and saves every reading with a photo in date-organised records. Businesses get fast entry checks and an audit trail ready for any inspection, with no staff needed at the door."},{"id":"k207","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Autonomous explorati","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/autonomous-exploration-mapping-robot/","text":"A robotics research and development client. Our autonomous robot explores spaces it has never seen. It heads for the edge of its current map (frontier-based exploration), labels rooms and objects with computer vision as it builds the map (semantic fusion), and calculates the shortest route home, with no prior map and no human guidance."},{"id":"k208","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI remote exam proct","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-remote-exam-proctoring-platform/","text":"An education provider running remote exams. A remote exam proctoring system for an education provider. It watches webcam, audio and typing behavior during the exam, checks identity with anti-spoofing face detection and keystroke biometrics, flags anomalies in real time, keeps an offline backup of answers and produces an integrity report with heatmaps afterwards."},{"id":"k209","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI task assistant fo","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/slack-ai-task-assistant-for-teams/","text":"A team-productivity software startup. An AI task assistant for teams. People describe work in plain language in Slack and the assistant creates the task, assigns it, predicts a deadline and priority, runs standups, sends reminders and syncs with Notion. Managers get a performance insights view without asking anyone for a status update."},{"id":"k210","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Real-time fleet trac","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/real-time-fleet-tracking-dashboard/","text":"A logistics operator running a vehicle fleet. A real-time fleet management dashboard for a logistics operator. It shows every vehicle live on a map, supports geofences and route playback, alerts on speeding, harsh braking and idling, and turns fuel data into reports. The streaming backend was built to handle hundreds of vehicles reporting at once."},{"id":"k211","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Retail demand foreca","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/retail-demand-forecasting-inventory-platform/","text":"A retailer with multiple product categories. A demand forecasting and inventory optimization platform for a multi-category retailer. Machine-learning models trained on sales history forecast demand with seasonality, simulate stock depletion and raise reorder alerts automatically. Buyers work from category dashboards and export the numbers for planning."},{"id":"k212","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Offline voice-to-voi","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/offline-voice-translation-mobile-app/","text":"A consumer mobile-app business. A mobile app that translates speech to speech, even without a connection. It chains speech recognition, translation and text-to-speech, uses compressed on-device models for offline language packs, and keeps conversation history in a chat-style view stored only on the phone, with no cloud sync."},{"id":"k213","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Gym management platf","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/gym-management-platform-member-app/","text":"A gym and fitness business. A gym management platform with a member mobile app. Staff manage members, trainers, schedules and payments in one back office; trainers upload workout and nutrition plans and chat with members in the app; renewal and payment reminders go out automatically, with billing handled by Stripe."},{"id":"k214","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Smart-grid monitorin","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/smart-grid-monitoring-fault-prediction/","text":"An electricity utility. A smart-grid monitoring system for an electricity utility. Low-power LoRa sensors stream readings into a time-series database, real-time dashboards show the state of the network, and anomaly-detection models predict faults and raise alerts. A REST API lets other utility systems use the data."},{"id":"k215","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): Face-recognition ent","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/face-recognition-access-attendance-system/","text":"A company managing access to its offices. A face-recognition entry and attendance system for offices. A Raspberry Pi terminal recognizes staff with anti-spoofing checks, logs attendance from each entry, alerts on unknown faces and unauthorized attempts, and keeps running offline. Managers review access and attendance in a reporting dashboard."},{"id":"k216","title":"Case studies (anonymous by policy: client names are never published): AI SEO article gener","url":"https://visionbotix.com/work/ai-seo-blog-content-generator/","text":"A content-marketing software startup. A generative AI writing product for SEO content. Users enter a topic, a keyword planner suggests terms with difficulty and volume, a GPT-4 pipeline built with LangChain drafts the article, an SEO audit checks it, and the result exports to HTML, Markdown or WordPress."},{"id":"k217","title":"Company","url":"https://visionbotix.com/","text":"- [About](https://visionbotix.com/about/) - [How we work](https://visionbotix.com/process/) - [Pricing](https://visionbotix.com/pricing/) - [Project cost estimator](https://visionbotix.com/estimate/) - [Contact](https://visionbotix.com/contact/) - [Careers](https://visionbotix.com/careers/)"},{"id":"k218","title":"Company","url":"https://visionbotix.com/","text":"- [Privacy policy](https://visionbotix.com/privacy/) - [Terms of use](https://visionbotix.com/terms/)"}];
